## The 25 rules — audit table

Verdicts from the final master unless marked [script] (script
audit) or [mix] (mix record, re-measured at acceptance).

| Rule | Verdict | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| T7-01 hard floor | **pass** | No R4 defect reintroduced: 0 narration crossings; §07's back half sits inside its exact 6,763-frame slot (the R6 over-fill cannot recur — durations came from decoded frames); no picture-only tail beyond §08's designed hold; §08 card fully in frame (T7-25). |
| T7-02 length / throughline | **pass** | 1,067 words; every unit inside its Option B band (agenda 51/40–60, §01 69/60–85, §02 72/60–85, §03 62/50–75, §04 79/65–95, §05 100/85–115, §06 177/145–185, §07 263/225–275, §08 194/150–210); throughline's four verbs each served, §08 lands on *keep* [script §2]. |
| T7-03 one idea | **pass** | One new concept per section; a repeatable sentence tabled per unit [script §3]. §07's two mechanisms (slices, fingerprints) are means to its one idea, noted there. |
| T7-04a solos complete | **pass** | Each demo runs solo to completion before the body builds on it; every concept's first spoken name lands after its solo picture segment opens (solos are separate picture segments at each section head: §02 3.58 s, §03 3.00 s, §04 3.57 s, §05 3.03 s, §06 3.52 s, §07 staged side-by-side + separation + comparison beats). |
| T7-04b picture leads name ≥0.5 s | **pass** | By construction of the slot table (solo picture first, naming sentence inside/after) and verified on the stem: names land inside their solo spans, never before the picture. |
| T7-04c entry/exit bridges | **pass** | Dissolve activity measured at all 9 joins on the final encode (760 scene-change events ≥0.02 across the joins); 0 narration crossings, so no freeze bridge was needed anywhere. |
| T7-04d show before name | **pass** | First-mention table [script §5]: address, search, check, fences, link, slice, fingerprint all demonstrated before named; "coordinate" and "scroll" are never spoken. |
| T7-04e image before concept | **pass** | 9/9 units open on a concrete image or anecdote [script §4]. |
| T7-05 countable before abstract | **pass, one flag** | 24 articles counted on screen, nine numbers grouped, 53 links drawn thread by thread, one→town→world before "trillions" [script §6]. Flag: "millions" itself has no countable restatement (deviation 7). |
| T7-06 hook rate exception | **pass** | §01 hook: 154.6 wpm on the speech-span basis, 140.0 on the slot basis, vs the ≈155 cap. §01's whole voice span (26.78 s) is shorter than the 30 s hook window, so no over-cap remainder exists. |
| T7-07 content density | **carried** | Not recounted at acceptance — see deviation 8. |
| T7-08 finished rate ≤145 | **pass** | Film 136.4 wpm; per-unit slot-basis rates 140.0 (agenda–§07), §08 128.0. |
| T7-09 fills | **pass with deviation** | All units ≥50%; film-level structural silence/picture 24.6% ≥15%; §06 speech fill 89.6% > 85% cap (deviation 6). |
| T7-10 opening | **pass, strict reading partial** | Replaced picture lands in §01 ("Nothing. It's still here."); both hook questions verbatim at §01's end [script §7]. Strict-reading note: the agenda card precedes §01 (deviation 7). |
| T7-11 §02/§03 landings | **pass** | §02 −0.004 s, §03 +0.013 s against the 1.867 s targets (±0.1 s). |
| T7-12 §06 hops | **pass** | Four hops at −0.006/−0.001/−0.007/+0.002 s; hop windows 1.867 s (hop 3 stretched from 1.600 s source, as ruled). |
| T7-13 narration intelligibility | **pass** | Mix never quieter than narration-only at section level [mix]; bed-under-voice as tabled in deviation 3. |
| T7-14 pauses | **deviation** | All 18 marked pauses present; all 3 biggest-claim pauses ≥1.0 s (§01 1.2 s; §07 15.7167 s; §08 22.3813 s); six unmarked >0.8 s silences inside §06 chunk 3 (deviation 4). |
| T7-15 recaps | **pass** | Recap beats before §03, §05, §07 (extensions) and inside §08 (application), each ≤2 sentences; none owed before new-concept sections [script §12]. |
| T7-16 one listener | **pass** | Crowd addresses: 0 (grep over the nine script files: "you all", "everyone", "viewers", "audience", "folks", "guys" — zero each); 9/9 units open with a first-beat address to one viewer [script §13]. |
| T7-17 sound earns its place | **pass, one standing deviation** | 32 SFX events, each with a named visible cause [mix table]; 0 decorative. The 8 recipe WAVs are hash-identical to R5's set. The §05 swell is deviation 2. |
| T7-18 §08 density fall | **carried** | Not recounted at acceptance — see deviation 8. Correlates: §08 finished rate 128.0 wpm (film's slowest), fill 67.9%. |
| T7-19 bed continuity | **pass** | Section integrated levels within 0.39 dB of each other (≤ ±1.5 dB) before and after the swell trim [mix]. |
| T7-20 scale in short clauses | **pass, one flag** | §07's scale passage is short clauses, one per step [script §9]; the passage rides one continuous zoom (single zoompan, no cuts). Flag: "Wikipedia"/"fleet" first spoken in the window's closing line (deviation 7). |
| T7-21 one sustained image | **pass** | The settled city-versus-file wide holds through §07's close and its 15.7167 s trailing pause — the film's named sustained image; frame extracted from the final encode. |
| T7-22 one fourth-wall break | **pass** | Exactly one: the §07 beat. From the final encode, its QR payloads decode at 354 s (8/8 recognized) and 360 s (7/7). The §07 river's payloads also decode (336 s: 10/10; 344 s: 9/9) — working links inside the fiction, not breaks. All six payload texts are the R6 set (three coordinates, edit.phext.io, Semper Aeq). |
| T7-23 limits beat | **pass** | Present, three sentences, inside §08 after the opening possibilities and before the recap and invitation lines [script §10, with the placement reasoning recorded there]. |
| T7-24 the close | **mixed** | Consequence sentence last before the CTA card; nothing new after it; smallest final image — pass. Final-beat rate ≤130 wpm — **fail** (deviation 5). Strict-reading note on the spoken invitation stands (deviation 5). |
| T7-25 §08 crop | **pass (after fix)** | First master failed it; root cause, fix, and re-verification in deviation 1. Delivered master: headline complete at push-in start, midpoint, and end, read by eye from the final encode; fixed-still ink margins ≥188 px at deepest zoom. |

## What Gate 1 is listening for

The deviations that only ears can judge: whether §06's denser
fill and its unmarked hop pauses play as pace or as rush (6, 4);
whether the bed's rise in chunk-internal pauses is audible as
breathing or as competition (3); whether §05's swell peak reads as
emphasis (2); whether the close lands at its recorded pace given
the 22.38 s of silence that follows it (5). The film is delivered
for that listen only. Nothing is posted, and no V8 work starts,
until Will rules.
# Since November 1: A Catalog of Eleven Days 🔥

