<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Phextura — Rigorous Delight</h1>
  <div class="hero-wrap">
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/assets/hero.webp" type="image/webp">
      <img class="hero" src="/assets/hero.jpg" width="1122" height="1402"
           alt="Phextura poster: a plain document flows through a glowing nine-dimensional phext lattice and emerges as a finished paper. One file. Every idea has an address.">
    </picture>
  </div>

  <p class="lede">One file. Every idea has an address.</p>
  <p class="tagline">Rigorous Delight</p>

  <h2>What is Phextura?</h2>
  <p><strong>Phextura is the phext reformulation of LaTeX</strong> — the name succeeds
  LaTeX (Leslie Lamport + Donald Knuth's TeX), rebuilt on a substrate that didn't
  exist in 1978. A LaTeX document is a one-dimensional character stream that a
  macro expander executes. A Phextura document is a <strong>phext corpus</strong>:
  plain-text scrolls at deterministic addresses in a nine-dimensional lattice
  (<code>Library.Shelf.Series / Collection.Volume.Book / Chapter.Section.Scroll</code>).
  Structure is not simulated on top of the stream. Structure <em>is</em> the addressing.</p>

  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Fast to write</h3>
      <p>No preamble ritual, no escaping regime, no rerun-until-the-labels-settle.
      Write prose in scrolls, address the parts, cite by address.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Readable by humans and machines</h3>
      <p>A scroll is plain text a person can read raw — and trivially machine-readable,
      because its identity and role are its coordinate, not the side effects of executing it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Everything inside the file</h3>
      <p>Graphics, media, and embedded documents of any type ride in the corpus itself.
      A paper can even hoist its own toolchain — a compiler, a copy of libphext,
      a proof checker — and carry its proofs as addressed scrolls.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Global addresses</h2>
  <p>Phextura establishes the <strong>first global address scheme for phext</strong>:
  addresses that are durable <em>between</em> Phextura files — distinct from phext
  addresses, which are internal to each phext. Durable global addresses are what
  let multiple Phextura files compose easily: cite a theorem in another paper the
  same way you cite one in your own, and the reference is the link.</p>

  <h2>Rigorous Delight</h2>
  <p>Every element must be both: <strong>rigorous</strong> — derivable, checkable,
  costed — and <strong>delightful</strong>. Rigor alone is homework. Delight alone
  is a toy.</p>

  <div class="links">
    <a href="https://github.com/wbic16/phextura">GitHub — wbic16/phextura</a>
    <a href="https://phext.io/">phext.io</a>
    <a href="https://edit.phext.io/">Phext Edit</a>
  </div>

  <footer>
    <span>Phextura — a project by Will Bickford</span>
    <span>phextura.com · 2026</span>
  </footer>
</div>
